From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] media: xilinx: csi2rxss: initialize media entity function

The Xilinx VIPP composite driver expects every subdevice entity in the media
graph to advertise a valid entity function. The vendor CSI-2 RX subsystem
driver registers its media entity without setting `entity.function`, which
causes graph construction to warn that the entity type was not initialized and
prevents the media topology from being fully registered.

Mark the CSI-2 RX subsystem as a video interface bridge before registering the
subdevice.

Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@openai.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/xilinx/xilinx-csi2rxss.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/xilinx/xilinx-csi2rxss.c b/drivers/media/platform/xilinx/xilinx-csi2rxss.c
index 7173f419df8a..45c3b92ae1d1 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/xilinx/xilinx-csi2rxss.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/xilinx/xilinx-csi2rxss.c
@@ -1124,6 +1124,7 @@ static int xcsi2rxss_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	subdev->dev = dev;
 	strscpy(subdev->name, dev_name(dev), sizeof(subdev->name));
 	subdev->flags |= V4L2_SUBDEV_FL_HAS_EVENTS | V4L2_SUBDEV_FL_HAS_DEVNODE;
+	subdev->entity.function = MEDIA_ENT_F_VID_IF_BRIDGE;
 	subdev->entity.ops = &xcsi2rxss_media_ops;
 	v4l2_set_subdevdata(subdev, xcsi2rxss);
 
